{
  "$comment": [
    "GH-738 (item 3bshch) - the emptiness map of the row a run assembles, measured on the bench.",
    "Values are not here on purpose: they move for lawful reasons every run. What must not move",
    "quietly is whether a key is EMPTY - `null -> filled` means a number appeared where the row",
    "used to say 'not known', which is a different sentence to whoever reads it.",
    "The case that called for it: GH-731 repaired the choice of sample, passed its acceptance, and",
    "the stored row went from `ecw null` to `ecw 0` because a stand-in elsewhere stopped being",
    "blocked. Every case was green: that drift was nobody's subject.",
    "Taken from what the run ASSEMBLED, before any write, so it answers even when no row has been",
    "stored since the change.",
    "Down to the leaves, not the sections: `ecw` lives inside `computed.waterBalance`, and a map of sections would have missed the very drift this exists for.",
    "GH-738 (the reviewer's return): the run's state is now assembled by the product's own `gaip_build_state`, not by a literal this file wrote, so the map is of the row the product would store. It grew from 422 keys to 540, and `computed.waterBalance.ecw` is among them because the site now has a water sample with a conductivity.",
    "GH-777 (queue item 4, slice 2): `computed.notApplicable` joins the row - the pass's third account, beside what it could not compute and what it said. It is a LIST, so 'filled' here means the key is there; whether it carries an entry is what the account itself is for."
  ],
  "ticket": "GH-738",
  "measuredOn": "the orchestrator bench as a run frame (?rerun=&site=), one assembled row",
